#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069609} :activity/id #uuid "8ab5b031-09a4-5e75-b365-2c7486f2168f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050975 :topic/id #uuid "7697398d-61ca-52dc-8fab-4d569b573455" :topic/math-academy-id 459} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069609 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186070033 :tutorial/content "To find the distance between two points on the Cartesian plane, we can create a right triangle and use the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nTo demonstrate, consider the points $(2, 3)$ and $(5, 7)$, shown in the diagram below. We draw a right triangle so that the segment between the two points is the hypotenuse.\n\n![](images/3d/3d3629fbd659ebfb6d32080feeb64bd2ebdd3fb63e9826970d64aa41a00b9a56.png)\n\nWe can find the distance between the points by finding the length of the hypotenuse $d$ using the Pythagorean theorem in the form\n\n$$\nd = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\n$$\n\nFrom this perspective:\n\n- $a$ is the distance between the $x$-coordinates.\n$a|= x_{2} - x_{1}; = 5 - 2; = 3$\n- $b$ is the distance between the $y$-coordinates.\n$b|= y_{2} - y_{1}; = 7 - 3; = 4$\n\nSo the distance between the points $(2, 3)$ and $(5, 7)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} d &= \\sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} \\\\[3pt] &= \\sqrt{9 + 16} \\\\[3pt] &= \\sqrt{25} \\\\[3pt] &= 5. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn general, the distance $d$ between any two points in the Cartesian plane is given by the **distance formula**:\n\n$$\nd = \\sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "e9d89e3c-10fa-540c-bc9f-221d84f3a839" :tutorial/math-academy-id 9120 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "8fd761d6-3af8-51f6-824f-a972e67c1b97" :step/math-academy-id 147701 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069610}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069610 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068720 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068508 :question/id #uuid "ca739248-c388-531e-ba5f-7f9cce2aa70b" :question/math-academy-id "e-14706"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5df52cb5-75b1-58d9-8535-07c1bb87be34" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049224} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049923}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069125} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069298} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069301} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233259} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233635} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235489} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523930} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523953}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of a Segment"} :step/id #uuid "0b810045-0fb8-56a2-8dbc-c8ee53eec31b" :step/math-academy-id 147702 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069611}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069611 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068721 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068509 :question/id #uuid "303019d6-7004-5de8-92e3-1119d4829ca8" :question/math-academy-id "e-14707"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdded031-fd95-5a7f-92d4-c0d6713ba64d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069126} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069136} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069299} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233458} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234007} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234145} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523992}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between Two Points"} :step/id #uuid "64a5b83b-0cea-5df2-83c0-47ab8dcad671" :step/math-academy-id 147706}] :activity/title "The Distance Formula" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068986}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524049} :activity/id #uuid "04dd10aa-617a-57e9-9def-004b4d0d2ea1" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050975 :topic/id #uuid "7697398d-61ca-52dc-8fab-4d569b573455" :topic/math-academy-id 459} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524049 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88eabd55-766f-573b-8305-9db9fb46fea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066977} {:answer/id #uuid "b827aac1-596d-54de-9317-02f420f5b264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066978} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9efbb1-7d26-572a-8d2c-c509a6d4a218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066979} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a39913-c29c-5674-8ad9-5afeccfbe7b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066980} {:answer/id #uuid "4e1c13fe-164d-597b-9a55-f85afdd238b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066981}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186066981} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f04668a-3df1-560e-950f-53985118bf87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "94652e83-5bd0-5884-9087-2e26389b0cf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-3717" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd878559d6be37faa60bdb33cbebe2f124d09744aa4df7dae40372499116f239.png)\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{CD}?$" :question/worked-solution "From the figure, we note that the points $C$ and $D$ have coordinates ${{(-5,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(2,-1)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})},$ respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{―}{CD},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-(-5))^{2}+(-1-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(7)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{65}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "31a02459-846b-594d-a08e-bf91b9b551fd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524050}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524050 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c855929-b300-53bb-b2f5-24705e47b13c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523443} {:answer/id #uuid "6221fb69-119d-504d-b579-13f039a770b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523452} {:answer/id #uuid "7c2e9f91-d463-5286-9ed4-c97a3b93b2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523513} {:answer/id #uuid "c60b17ee-f26e-5eec-9f8d-f02e776c1ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523671} {:answer/id #uuid "ebbeab2f-2e72-502f-8588-62b91c0340f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523747}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523747} :answer-field/id #uuid "8db667e4-c6ff-50ef-bf4d-33616aab5cf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9dd278e6-83f6-5c4b-b1f1-6a6ae9e2e467" :question/math-academy-id "q-119011" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(-4\\sqrt{5},-2\\sqrt{5})$ and $(\\sqrt{5},-12\\sqrt{5})?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have ${{(-4\\sqrt{5},-2\\sqrt{5})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(\\sqrt{5},-12\\sqrt{5})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\nSo, the distance $d$ can be calculated using the distance formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{5}-(-4\\sqrt{5}))}^{2}+{(-12\\sqrt{5}-(-2\\sqrt{5}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5\\sqrt{5})^{2}+(-10\\sqrt{5})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25(5)+100(5)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125+500} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{625} \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "31c22abb-16d4-5821-a52d-1bfe8c5323e2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524067}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186524067 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a941df4e-944d-5b40-96d0-15089e219a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523612}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523612} :answer-field/id #uuid "69167d57-152a-5b5e-a04c-0fa20c63b0b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "10bae273-6993-5b75-9a9e-139dcefc8633" :question/math-academy-id "q-216294" :question/problem "![](images/94/941efa39e90b946e68ea9ccc65ab7b97f4fce84d1cccbaa19135f8c87383a22f.png)\n\nThe exact length of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "From the figure, we note that the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates ${{(-2,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(2,7)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})},$ respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{―}{AB},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-(-2))^{2}+(7-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{32} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "6cdce9b7-05c1-5e9f-8efe-1d31cef1a31b"}] :activity/title "The Distance Formula" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523236}]}
